\begin{abstract}
The Pathological Simulation Core (PS\_BP\_001A) is an integrated hardware engine that combines
ultra-high-performance fiber-reinforced concrete (UHPFRC) structural containment, titanium
core casings, hardened cryptographic processors, high-density pathogen simulation engines,
bio-interface sensor arrays, and quantum-adjacent optical interconnects into a single
coherent system. This white sheet presents the dimensional blueprint verification, materials
characterization, optical and cryptographic performance, biological simulation stability,
and structural shielding properties. Empirical results indicate that the system operates
at or near theoretical limits in multiple domains simultaneously, suggesting a new class
of engineered matter and computational architecture.
\end{abstract}

\section{System Architecture Overview}

\subsection{Geometric Envelope and Core Layout}
The primary assembly length is
\[
L_{\text{total}} = \SI{1250}{\milli\meter},
\]
with an outer cross-section of
\[
W \times H = \SI{450}{\milli\meter} \times \SI{360}{\milli\meter}.
\]
Section A--A defines an internal octagonal bore of nominal diameter
\[
\varnothing_{\text{bore}} = \SI{500}{\milli\meter},
\]
with tolerance $+0.00/-0.03\ \si{\milli\meter}$.

Four titanium core casings (Ti-6Al-4V Grade 5) are seated within the bore, each aligned
with a nominal circumferential clearance gap of
\[
g_{\text{align}} = \SI{2.00}{\milli\meter} \pm \SI{0.01}{\milli\meter},
\]
providing vibration decoupling and thermal expansion margin.

\subsection{Functional Subsystems}
The system integrates:
\begin{itemize}
  \item Hardened cryptographic processor (AES-256 / AE9-256 ASIC).
  \item Pathology analyzer and pathogen simulation algorithm engine (FPGA/ASIC hybrid).
  \item Bio-interface sensor arrays (4$\times$ quartz--lithium niobate transducers).
  \item Dual single-mode polarization-maintaining fiber-optic interfaces.
  \item UHPFRC + basalt fiber outer chassis with radiation shielding fillers.
  \item Mu-metal and copper EMI/RFI containment and OFHC micro-channel cold plates.
\end{itemize}

