\section{Materials Science: UHPFRC Composite}

\subsection{Mix Design and Physical Properties}
The outer chassis employs an ultra-high-performance fiber-reinforced concrete (UHPFRC)
with basalt micro-fibers and heavy-aggregate shielding fillers:
\begin{align*}
\rho_{\text{matrix}} &= \SI{2850}{\kilogram\per\cubic\meter},\\
\text{w/b} &= 0.16,\\
V_{\text{fiber}} &= 2.5\% \text{ (steel/basalt hybrid, } \varnothing \SI{0.2}{\milli\meter} \times \SI{13}{\milli\meter}).
\end{align*}
Curing protocol: \SI{24}{\hour} at \SI{20}{\celsius} (moist cure), followed by \SI{48}{\hour}
steam autoclave at \SI{90}{\celsius}, 100\% RH.

\subsection{Mechanical Performance}
Uniaxial compressive strength tests on $\varnothing \SI{100}{\milli\meter} \times \SI{200}{\milli\meter}$ cores:
\begin{align*}
P_{\max} &= \SI{1610}{\kilo\newton},\\
f_c &= \SI{205.0}{\mega\pascal}.
\end{align*}
Flexural performance (three-point bending on prism specimens):
\begin{align*}
